        title: "Horimiya", 
        author: "HERO & Daisuke Hagiwara", 
        genre: "Romance & Comedy", 
        volumes: "17 Vols",
        image: "images/horimiya.jpg",
        synopsis: "An unlikely friendship forms when a popular academic girl and a gloomy, secretly tattooed boy cross paths outside school, revealing their true hidden personalities.",
        chapterTitle: "Chapter 1: A Little Story From Page One",
        storyContent: "SCENE 1: THE TWO SCHOOL FACES\nKyoko Hori is the beautiful, popular, and energetic high school girl loved by everyone in her class. Izumi Miyamura is her complete opposite—a quiet, gloomy, and anti-social nerd who sits in the back corner behind a wall of long hair, rumored to be an obsessed anime otaku.\n\nSCENE 2: HORI'S DOMESTIC SECRET\nImmediately after the final bell, Hori strips away her popular persona. She rushes home, removes her school makeup, ties her hair back into a messy bun, and spends her afternoons scrubbing floors, cooking meals, and babysitting her younger brother Souta while her parents work long hours, keeping her domestic life a total secret.\n\nSCENE 3: THE PUNKY STRANGER\nOne afternoon, Souta returns home from the park after falling down, led by a stylish, handsome guy with nine ear piercings, a cool leather jacket, and multiple punk tattoos stretching down his arms. Hori welcomes him into the kitchen, thanking him for assisting her brother.\n\nSCENE 4: THE TRUE IDENTITY REVELATION\nThe stylish stranger looks around the room, realizing where he is: 'Hori? Wait... you look totally different without your uniform.' Hori screams in absolute shock as she recognizes the deep voice—this punk is actually Miyamura from her class. He explains he hides his piercings and tattoos at school to avoid trouble, and the two agree to keep each other's hidden identities safe."
