        title: "Pluto", 
        author: "Naoki Urasawa", 
        genre: "Mystery & Supernatural", 
        volumes: "8 Vols",
        image: "images/pluto.jpg",
        synopsis: "A robotic Europol detective investigates a string of high-profile murders targeting the world's seven most advanced robots and their human creators.",
        chapterTitle: "Chapter 1: Gesicht",
        storyContent: "SCENE 1: THE FALL OF MONT BLANC\nIn a highly advanced future where humans and artificial intelligence coexist under strict laws, Mont Blanc—a legendary, mountain-tending robot and one of the world's seven most advanced humanoids—is found brutally destroyed in a Swiss forest. His chassis is torn apart, and his head is impaled with a pair of massive, primitive wooden horns.\n\nSCENE 2: INVESTIGATING THE HORNS\nGesicht, an elite humanoid detective working for Europol, is assigned to lead the investigation. He uses his advanced internal scanners to analyze the crime scene, realizing the attacker possessed terrifying physical power capable of shattering military-grade titanium alloys with bare hands.\n\nSCENE 3: THE HUMAN CULPRIT LINK\nShortly after, a prominent human pro-robot activist is found murdered in his high-rise apartment in Germany. The local police find identical horn shapes carved into the plaster wall right above his body. Gesicht realizes the killer is specifically executing the key veteran figures of the recent Central Asian war.\n\nSCENE 4: THE ROBOTIC WARNING\nGesicht reviews the forensic data matrix, concluding that the killer's behavioral subroutines do not align with human movement profiles. He realizes a terrifying, god-like rogue entity is hunting the world's elite AI. Looking out over the city lights, Gesicht's core processors send a system alert warning: 'The killer is a robot. And I am next on its list.'"
