        genre: "Cyberpunk & Mecha", 
        volumes: "14 Vols",
        image: "images/evangelionc.jpg",
        synopsis: "A reluctant teenage boy is forced by his cold father to pilot a colossal biomechanical weapon to protect humanity from mysterious alien entities called Angels.",
        chapterTitle: "Chapter 1: Angel Attack",
        storyContent: "SCENE 1: THE EMPTY HIGHWAY\nIn the fortress city of Tokyo-3, 14-year-old Shinji Ikari stands by a concrete phone booth, checking his transit maps as air raid sirens wail across empty, evacuated highways. Out in the ocean, a massive, towering entity known as the Third Angel emerges, unaffected by military tanks and artillery fire.\n\nSCENE 2: THE UNDEGROUND COMPLEX\nMisato Katsuragi rescues Shinji in her car just as a massive missile detonation shakes the highway. She drives him deep underground into NERV Headquarters, a massive subterranean dome. There, Shinji is confronted by his cold, estranged father, Commander Gendo Ikari.\n\nSCENE 3: THE FLOATING GIANT\nGendo guides him to a massive flooded bay where Evangelion Unit-01—a terrifying, purple bio-mechanical giant weapon—floats in containment fluid. Gendo commands Shinji to pilot the machine immediately to engage the Angel, revealing he only summoned his son because of his genetic synchronization compatibility markers.\n\nSCENE 4: PILOT INITIALIZATION\nShinji breaks down weeping, refusing to enter the machine, until Gendo coldly orders the heavily bandaged, bleeding clone girl Rei Ayanami to take his place instead. Unable to watch her suffer, Shinji relents, climbing into the entry plug capsule cockpit. As the amber LCL fluid floods the tank and his brain waves sync with the giant, Shinji grips the controls, repeating a desperate chant: 'I mustn't run away... I mustn't run away...'"
